# Note Schema

## Project Memory

`project_memory/` is the durable cross-run memory. It is snapshotted into each run and should be updated cautiously.

### canonical_summary.md

Current best understanding of the problem, definitions, bottlenecks, and live strategic picture. Keep it concise enough to fit in context.

### claim_ledger.md

Use one entry per nontrivial claim:

```text
## Claim: <short name>
Status: conjecture | plausible | refuted | proven | external-known-result
Confidence: low | medium | high
Dependencies:
Evidence:
Known gaps:
Critiques:
Next checks:
Source:
```

### lemma_bank.md

Candidate lemmas, proved lemmas, reductions, and reusable technical tools. Every lemma should state assumptions and whether it is proved, conjectural, or externally known.

### failed_attempts.md

Failed approaches with enough detail to avoid repeating them. Include the obstruction or missing step.

### counterexamples.md

Counterexamples, toy instances, edge cases, and obstruction patterns.

### literature_map.md

Known results, papers, authors, search terms, related problem names, and source-grounded summaries.

### promising_directions.md

Live directions to explore next. Include why each direction is promising and what would falsify it.

### bibliography.md

Bibliographic entries and links. Prefer source URLs, arXiv identifiers, DOI links, and short notes about relevance.

## Per-Run Reports

Every worker report should contain:

```text
# <Role> Report

## Summary
## Concrete Progress
## Claims Or Lemmas
## Gaps And Risks
## Counterexamples Or Obstructions
## Sources Consulted
## Recommended Next Steps
```

Critic reports should classify issues as:

```text
fatal gap | missing assumption | false claim | unsupported citation | plausible but incomplete | worth pursuing
```

The final run memo should separate:

```text
Accepted progress
Candidate routes
Refuted or weakened claims
Useful failed attempts
Recommended next run
Project memory update proposal
```

